# Trim the build context for packaging/container/Dockerfile.
# The image builds only: spdk/, rados-nkvx/, clients/nvme-kv/, scripts/,
# packaging/, and the top-level license/version files. Everything below is
# large and unused by the build (weights, VM images, the CMake build tree, git).

.git
build/
vm-images/

# clients/: keep only nvme-kv (the kv_shim the RPM spec builds).
clients/vllm-weights/
clients/rkv/
clients/vm/
clients/nixl/
clients/rocm-xio/

# Empty submodule placeholders not used by the container build.
ceph/

# The Dockerfile and build scripts are not consumed inside the image (the RPM
# spec only reads packaging/rpm/*). Excluding them keeps the `COPY . /src` layer
# cache stable across Dockerfile edits, so tweaking a late step does not force a
# full SPDK recompile.
packaging/container/Dockerfile
packaging/container/build.sh
packaging/container/build-clean.sh

# SPDK host-build artifacts must NOT enter the context. The Dockerfile compiles
# SPDK (and vendors Mercury) from clean sources; shipping the host's build trees
# breaks the build because cmake/meson caches bake in absolute host paths
# (/home/kyle/...) and abort when re-run under /src. All of the below are
# git-ignored generated output in the spdk submodule.
spdk/build/
spdk/dpdk/build/
spdk/dpdk/build-tmp/
spdk/vendor/
spdk/mk/config.mk
spdk/**/*.o
spdk/**/*.d
spdk/**/*.a
spdk/**/*.so
spdk/**/*.so.*
spdk/**/.libs/
